cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Visual Stimulator in your research, please cite this software and the version used."
title: "Visual Stimulator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Milla Navarro"
    given-names: "Santi"
version: "2.1.3"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
url: "https://github.com/SantiMillaNavarro/Visual-Stimulator"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SantiMillaNavarro/Visual-Stimulator"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >-
  Open scientific software for controlled and reproducible visual stimulation
  in experimental research. Visual Stimulator can be used in MEA and other
  electrophysiology workflows, ex vivo retinal or tissue preparations, in vivo
  experiments, and other setups requiring controlled display-based visual
  stimulation, with optional TTL synchronization and per-frame timing records.
keywords:
  - visual stimulation
  - electrophysiology
  - MEA
  - neuroscience
  - in vivo
  - ex vivo
  - PsychoPy
  - TTL synchronization
